  "question": {
    "text": "If the area covered by <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> from <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> to <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></math> is <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ln</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math>&nbsp;sq. units,&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
